{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1138914-c20-chimerical-items-question","id":1138914,"title":"C20 chimerical items question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-09T09:42:53-07:00","id":1138914,"title":"C20 chimerical items question","content":"I have a question about chimerical items in changeling. So if one stabs a changeling with a mundane knife that has a chimerical knife attached to it does it mean that the target gets both mundane and chimerical damage? Also can someone take a rifle in the Dreaming and use it there(in the Dreaming both chimerical and mundane damage are the same right?) <br /> In general I can't really get a grip on how chimerical items work and what's the point of them, besides interacting with things that are purely chimerical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13419-shirleymoor","name":"ShirleyMoor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T13:03:52-07:00","id":1138975,"title":"","content":"I never played nor hosted a game of Changeling, but I also tried to understand those questions and I know how hard/weird they can look. After a lot of thinking and readying, on the books and on the forum, I believe the answers for your questions are:<br /> <br /> 1) Yes, it does. If the knife is both real and chimerical, than he takes both damages. The same goes for anything chimerical with a real counterpart, so, if there is a chimerical sword with a real stick counterpart, then it gives the sword damage in lethal chimerical and stick damage in bashing real. But, as far as I understood, most chimerical items have no real counterpart.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, someone could shoot stuff with a real rifle in the Dreaming. But, for some reason, firearms doesnt behave very well on the Dreaming (something about chemistry being a weird thing for the Dreaming), and that is why there is no firearms treasures. I think the ideia is &quot;the dream like old-style or outlandish stuff&quot; and modern firearms are too real and banal. But it would work. I also would consider that firearms have a more &quot;outlandish&quot; or &quot;cinematic&quot; effect while on the Dreaming (making minions miss the bright side of a mountain, Rambo style, when shooting at the Heros or the Big Villains, or it suddenly has a very far shooting distance, if the shooter stops to aim for a while) as it is affect by the local glamour and peoples dreams of guns. (Also, dont forget that in the Dreaming the bullets would give Chimerical Lethal damage, which any fae can absorb with Stamina).<br /> <br /> 3) It works as objects invisible and inexistent to the rest of the world, but very real for Changelings. A Redcap with a big chimerical axe is a real danger for the unlucky Sidhe that he decided to stalk, but for the rest of the world, it is just a weird kid that looks like holding a imaginary weapon. It helps with the point of the &quot;invisible world&quot; and &quot;imaginary reality&quot; that is a big point in Changeling. For the Changeling, chimerical stuff is as real as everything else, so they would carry and work with it as usual, but they need always worry if there is somebody looking, as their banality can severely affect it, maybe even destroying it.<br /> <br /> I also don't know the full rules for them. I remember (or I think I remember) in editions past that Chimerical items could actually affect reality if no banal creature where looking, but if anybody looked at it, it would stop working (as it isnt actually real) and the changeling would gain banality (which I think is a far cooler concept than &quot;it doesn't affect reality at all&quot;). Also I dont know how some situations would work. In the following example:<br /> <br /> - A Troll fill up his real backpack with Chimerical Iron Ingots in the dreaming, and he wants to take it to his Knocker friend on the other side of the city so he can make a new fancy sword and a cool shield. He can carry it okay, as it is heavy but he is strong.<br /> <br /> 1 - When he gets on reality, does he bag look filled and heavy? Or do it look like regular?<br /> 1.1 - If the bag look heavy, would it stop looking heavy if someone looked inside and see it empty?<br /> 2 - If someone try to look inside, or try to weight it, it would be actually empty, but would the Troll have a banality trigger for carrying something &quot;Chimerically Heavy&quot;?<br /> 3 - If someone try to fill up the backpack with regular oranges, what would happen with the ingots? Would it disappear, corroded by banality, or would it coexist in the same space as the oranges?<br /> 3.1 - If it coexist, would any changeling that is aware of this situation get a banality trigger?<br /> 4 - If someone shake the backpack, opening down, throwing the ingots over a table full of expensive chinas, would it just bounce harmlessly off the china?<br /> 4.1 - If someone took a plate with a Iron Ingot over it and, inadvertently, carry it away, would the Ingot be carried away?<br /> <br /> I have some personal answers for those questions, but I'm not quite sure how official they are.<br /> <br /> Hope I helped you ShirleyMoor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T14:19:00-07:00","id":1138994,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Manbat! This clarifies things mostly. <br /> As for weapons in the Dreaming, I just don't want my players to take boring guns and explosives to the Dreaming, so I'll stick to weird working chemistry theory. <br /> As for chimerical items and their mundane counterparts and chimerical only items there's still so many weird things about real world interaction that I'm struggling to understand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13419-shirleymoor","name":"ShirleyMoor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T16:39:48-07:00","id":1139042,"title":"","content":"i always assumed that there were more recent chimerical firearms in the dreaming and the nobility were just purists (the cowboy's gun, the laser rifle, the A-team's unusually light chain gun ect.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T17:00:57-07:00","id":1139049,"title":"","content":"By rule, as far as I know, there are no firearms. They jump straight to sci-fi weapons. But I consider that new Nockers and Boggans can and are working in more modern equipment (as modern as WW2, sixties spy gadgets, etc.), of all kinds, not just weapons (like cars, tanks, air-planes, etc.) but the Dreaming somewhat resists it (as it is very traditionalist).<br /> <br /> But anything too chemical, like C4 or modern bombs, the dream can't work with, as people dont dream of Chemistry. But Dynamites certainly is something different.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T17:47:19-07:00","id":1139057,"title":"","content":"There actually are Chimerical firearms, up to and including Chimerical machineguns, that are bought as Treasures of varying levels, 2 for pistols/revolvers, 3 for heavy pistols/rifles and 4 for the aforementioned machineguns. These can be found in the Kithbook Nockers p.61.<br /> <br /> They are difficult to make and as such rare, and atleast in 2nd edition mostly a Nocker monopoly but then again their Birthright was a bit different back then.<br /> <br /> Nockers also make more sci-fi or steampunk weaponry like the lightning gun aswell as some oldschool repeating crossbows Etc.<br /> <br /> Steamtech used to be all the hoot in 2nd ed as steamengines worked extremely well in the Dreaming and so they have everything from steampowered power suits to airplanes and other warmachines. Again all of this can be found in Kithbook Nockers.<br /> <br /> Like said many Chimerical items do not have a real world counterpart and hence tend to not function when in the precense of the unenchanted and can create situations that invite Banality triggers. But while the Chimerical knife is useless against that loaf of bread, as well as it is against the unenchanted fellow next to you it can still cut you or your kithain buddy with Chimerical damage. I have generally ruled that once the unenchanted fellow leaves, or is enchanted, you are able to use it against that dastardly loaf of bread, but I do admit that it is likely a bit of house ruling on my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}